    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing, anchored by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (80.22) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against a left-handed arm, while **Cole Carrigg** sees a massive boost thanks to an ideal park environment and a targetable opposing starter in Lugo, S, making them our premier plays. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a foundational lock despite a challenging draw against Wheeler; his elite score (68.30) is bolstered significantly by park factors and a strong platoon split, ensuring he maintains value even when facing high-end pitching. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** and **Nasim Nunez** provide necessary speed and production, with **Nasim Nunez** leveraging a high-leverage SP matchup (4.93 xERA) to secure a strong 64.27 efficiency rating.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day involved **Luis Lara**, whose 50.28 score hovered just outside the starting rotation. While **Luis Lara** possesses the switch-hitting versatility and favorable SP matchup required for inclusion, the depth of our outfield and the efficiency of **Jackson Merrill** (63.41) ultimately crowded him out of the lineup. Meanwhile, **Wade Meckler** and **Denzer Guzman** fell well below the 40-point efficiency floor, largely due to the intimidating presence of Misiorowski on the mound; keeping them benched is a strategic necessity to preserve our game caps for more favorable sequences. \n\nRisks remain, particularly with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who both face pitchers boasting elite strikeout or suppression metrics that could deflate their daily returns. While **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** offer solid catching production, their scores are heavily dependent on immediate plate appearance efficiency. Managers should monitor any late weather shifts, as the park factors driving up the scores for **Cole Carrigg** and **Gunnar Henderson** are highly sensitive to wind patterns; otherwise, the lineup is optimized to maximize both counting stats and our critical stolen base requirements.",
